-- title:
--   Igusa nodes over supersingular places along level transports
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$ and $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ consisting exactly of the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with value of the geometric $j$-generator in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$), let $F = \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M' = \mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, and assume the base-changed full-level field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le F$. Further data: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ whose residue computes coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series over $A$; a primitive $q$-th root of unity index $\zeta$; valuation subrings $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ of $F$ indexed by $\ell \in \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ indexed by $s \in W$, subject to: $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$ is the Gauss-type ring $\{f : \exists x,y$ Laurent series over $A$, $\bar y \ne 0$, $f y = x\}$; each $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ is the pullback of $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\gamma \bmod q)\cdot\infty = \ell$; $\ell \mapsto \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_\ell$ is injective and permuted by all pullbacks along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$); each $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ induces $A$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, is fixed by all these pullbacks, contains an element $t$ with $t - a$ a unit for every $a \in A$, and receives the elements of $R_0$'s integer ring which are regular wherever the base-changed $j$ is regular and whose $R_0$-residue is $s$-integral, with the expected congruence modulo the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{ss}}_s$ at points of $A$ specialising to the value of that residue at $s$. Finally, let $R$ be a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from $F$ to $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$ with $R.\mathrm{integers} = \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$, let $R_0$'s integer ring be exactly the functions landing in $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{Ig}}_{\infty}$, let $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ be a finite set of places of the reduced full-level field over $\kappa$ with $|N^{\mathrm{Ig}}| = |W|$ admitting a ring homomorphism $j$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ compatible with the residues of $R_0$ and $R$ and characterising $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ as the places lying over some $s \in W$ through $j$, and let $g_\ell$ be automorphisms of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying in the subgroup generated by all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ ($\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$) and of the form $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $(\gamma \bmod q)\cdot\infty = \ell$. Then there is a family of places $x(\ell,s)$ of the reduced full-level field over $\kappa$, for $\ell \in \mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ and $s \in W$, all lying in $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$, such that for each $\ell$ there is a ring homomorphism $j_\ell$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ to that field which is compatible with $R_0$ and $R$ after transport by $g_\ell$ (for $f$ in $R_0$'s integer ring, $g_\ell(f)$ is $R$-integral with $R$-residue $j_\ell(R_0\text{-residue of } f)$), which pulls the valuation subring of $x(\ell,s)$ back to that of $s$ for every $s \in W$, which is $\kappa$-linear, and for which $N^{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is again exactly the set of places lying over some $s \in W$ through $j_\ell$.
--
--   This is a step in the construction of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve at $q$: it transports the nodes of the chart at $\infty$, which lie over the supersingular places of the level-$M'$ curve in characteristic $q$, along the level automorphisms realising the other lines of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, producing for each Igusa component a $\kappa$-linear reduction map and the full characterisation of the node set. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted).
